This crate is a Rust implementation of PP-OCR's networks and of the image
work around them, provided under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The parts named in
sections 2 and 3 are translated from OpenCV and Clipper source code and keep
those licences, reproduced at the end of this file. Everything else
reproduces the results of the projects below, measured by running them and
from their documentation, or is credited in sections 6 and 7. Preserve
LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and this notice.

1. RapidOCR (Apache-2.0), whose PP-OCR pipeline defines the steps, their
   parameters and their order. https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR

2. OpenCV. https://opencv.org
   resize, findContours, boxPoints, fillPoly and warpPerspective are
   reproduced from their results. findContours implements S. Suzuki and
   K. Abe, "Topological structural analysis of digitized binary images by
   border following", Computer Vision, Graphics, and Image Processing
   30(1), 1985.
   Translated to Rust from OpenCV 4.x source and changed:
   - src/geometry.rs, hull_order: the cyclic shift that convexHull applies
     to its hull indices (modules/imgproc/src/convhull.cpp, notice A);
   - src/geometry.rs, calipers: the rotating calipers of minAreaRect
     (modules/imgproc/src/rotcalipers.cpp, notice B);
   - src/crop.rs, cubic_weights: the INTER_CUBIC weights of
     interpolateCubic (modules/imgproc/src/imgwarp.cpp, notice C).

3. Clipper 6.4.2 by Angus Johnson, run through pyclipper 1.4.
   http://www.angusj.com
   src/geometry.rs, unclip: the round-joined corner offsets of
   ClipperOffset (OffsetPoint, DoRound) are translated to Rust from
   clipper.cpp and changed (notice D).

4. numpy (BSD-3-Clause) and shapely/GEOS (BSD-3-Clause, LGPL-2.1): the order
   of floating-point operations in normalisation, summation, area and length.

5. PaddleOCR (Apache-2.0): the PP-OCR models. tests/fixtures/characters.txt
   is the character list stored in the PP-OCRv6 small recogniser, and the
   plans a package installs are exported from the PP-OCRv6 small models
   RapidOCR distributes; both keep the models' licence.
   https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR
   No model weights are included. tools/export_ocr.py converts model files
   you obtain yourself; the plans it writes stay under the model's licence,
   and whoever redistributes them carries that licence with them.

6. Kernel family and SIMD tiering of src/engine/kernels/.
   The register-blocked transposed matrix-vector kernel, the runtime tier
   dispatch (AVX2+FMA / AVX / SSE4.1 / scalar) and the 64-byte weight
   alignment derive from the BigLinux
   `dpdfnet-native` package (MIT OR Apache-2.0), which derives them from
   `deepfilternet-quantized-ladspa` (MIT OR Apache-2.0). That package
   credits DeepFilterNet: Hendrik Schröter, Tobias Rosenkranz, Alberto N.
   Escalante-B. and Andreas Maier (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
   https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet

7. XNNPACK (BSD-3-Clause), by Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates and Google
   LLC. The folded sigmoid and the exponential under the softmax, GELU and
   swish compute as XNNPACK's f32-vsigmoid "p5-div" kernels do for finite
   values: the same constants, argument reduction and order of operations,
   written anew in Rust. https://github.com/google/XNNPACK


